{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from","id":1530138,"title":"[W5] Fixing the Cult of Fenris and creating the tribe it sprung from","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-06T22:51:46-08:00","id":1530138,"title":"[W5] Fixing the Cult of Fenris and creating the tribe it sprung from","content":"<b><i>[My first attempt posting this thread was flagged as &quot;unapproved&quot; because I tried to edit the OP. Mods: Please feel free to delete the &quot;unapproved&quot; thread.]</i></b><br /> <br /> This thread is another spinoff from my previous threads (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system\">here </a>and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk\">here</a>) about about house ruling W5. (By the way, in case anyone is interested, you can find the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/ri3cd7xbojkygta659ie6/House-Rules-v3.2.pdf?rlkey=82t417tvlqn9iysu0a4lkzr8w&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">latest version of my house rules </a>[PDF, Dropbox link] here.)<br /> <br /> As the title state, in this thread, I would like to revise the Cult of Fenris. But before I can develop them any further, I need to better understand where they came from.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, for this expansion of the house rules, I will follow these two premises:<ul><li>The Cult of Fenris is a fanatical Apocalypse cult of Garou, many of whom have fallen into hauglosk (as redefined in the house rules).</li> <li>While Garou from all tribes joined the Cult of Fenris, a lot of the foundational members came from one particular tribe. I don't have a name for this particular tribe yet, so I'll call them the [Get] for now.</li> </ul><br /> My goals for these house rules will be as follows:<ul><li>I'd like to stick to the general ideas and design philosophy behind 5th edition and W5; this includes that WtA is a reboot, not a continuation from legacy editions.</li> <li>I want to create the [Get] in a way that makes the development of the Cult plausible, but not inevitable.</li> <li>The [Get] should retain some recognizable elements of the Get of Fenris, but they should have their own niche in the setup of W5 tribes and be independent of human ethnicities or geographical regions.</li> </ul><br /> Again, I will build on something awesome posted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a>, that is, this fantastic <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526560#post1526560\">break-down of the tribes </a>in W5. I switched the Silent Striders and Glass Walkers, however, so it looks like this now:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MsoTableGrid\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>GLORY</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(aspirational future goal)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>HONOR</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(contributing to society)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"color:#2980b9\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>WISDOM</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(occult secrets)</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"color:#8e44ad\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>STEALTH</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(secrecy, subterfuge)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Shadow Lords</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(<span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Envision</span>, Intimidate, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Plan</span>, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Scheme</span>)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Bone Gnawers</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(<span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Eavesdrop</span>, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Infiltrate</span>, Pilfer, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Witness</span>)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Silent Striders</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(Deliver, Journey, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Sabotage</span>, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Scout</span>)</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"color:#8e44ad\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>CONFRONTATION</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(engage enemies)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Black Furies</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(<span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Avenge</span>, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Demolish</span>, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Dismantle</span>, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Overcome</span>)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Galestalkers</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(Ambush, Harry, Pursue, Track)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Ghost Council</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(Seek, Solve, Subvert, Unearth)</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"color:#8e44ad\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>COMMUNITY</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(benefit the Garou)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><u><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">[Get]</span></u></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Silver Fangs</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(<span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Inspire</span>, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Lead</span>, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Motivate</span>, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Rally</span>)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Glass Walkers</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(<span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Build</span>, Hack, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Repurpose</span>, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Research</span>)</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"color:#8e44ad\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>PROTECTION</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(defending)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Hart Wardens</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(<span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Cultivate</span>, Nurture, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Protect</span>, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Reclaim</span>)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Red Talons</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(<span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Purge</span>, Reduce, Ruin, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Ward</span>)</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>Children of Gaia</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(Discern, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Discover</span>, <span style=\"color:#8e44ad\">Heal</span>, <span style=\"color:#2980b9\">Puzzle Out</span>)</span></td> </tr> </table></div> This table leaves a specific spot for the [Get].<br /> <br /> My ideas are still in the beginning stage. What I have so far is the following:<ul><li>The [Get's] patron is Winter Wolf. In legacy, Winter Wolf was a totem of wisdom (or war) and associated with survival in harsh conditions, fierceness, and grit. I think this thematically well (and is a good connection back to the Get of Fenris and their ideology), and makes it possible that Fenris was a servant of Winter Wolf.</li> <li>Considering the Glory/Community spot left in the table and the choice of tribe patron, I envision this tribe as Garou who view themselves<ul><li>as conquerors of new territory and vanquishers of enemies, even under the most adverse conditions (GLORY),</li> <li>as enforcers who keep order and control among other Garou (COMMUNITY),</li> <li>as role models and teachers who use conflict and adversity to forge other Garou into perfection, increasing their prowess and survivability (COMMUNITY).</li> </ul></li> </ul>With regard to tribe verbs, I have generated a few that might fit the general idea:<ul><li>Enforce / Control</li> <li>Conquer / Expand / Subject</li> <li>Endure / Resist / Prevail</li> <li>Harden / Forge / Train</li> </ul>So, the idea is that the [Get] see themselves as the Garou's vanguard, forging the way for all the other tribes, teaching them how to be the perfect Garou (by being a role model and shaping them in a &quot;growth through adversity&quot; kind of way). At the same time, the seeds of authoritarianism and combativeness inherent in their self-identity is also what drove a lot of them into hauglosk.(I also imagine that, for the Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs, they often were useful idiots, more than willing to enforce their rules while seeing themselves as keeping order and helping the Garou Nation to remain united and strong.)<br /> <br /> What do you think?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T07:58:09-08:00","id":1530162,"title":"","content":"Hm. I think the Winter Wolf may be the wrong pick here - The Winter is a hard time, not a time for war, but a time for survival and getting through the long night. While Wolves are well equipped to handle the cold, Winter is marked by the fact that prey is lean and that it's a struggle to get through it into a more bountiful time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T08:43:32-08:00","id":1530164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530162#post1530162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I think the Winter Wolf may be the wrong pick here - The Winter is a hard time, not a time for war, but a time for survival and getting through the long night. While Wolves are well equipped to handle the cold, Winter is marked by the fact that prey is lean and that it's a struggle to get through it into a more bountiful time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, that was kind of my general idea--getting away a little bit from the Get of Fenris as the ultimate warriors to the [Get] being badass survivalists who seek adversity to burn away any remaining weakness in them. That being their ethos, I saw their role in Garou society both as vanguard/shock troops, as community enforcers, and as martial and athletic teachers.<br /> <br /> However, I'm still very open to completely alternative ideas. So, if you have another good suggestion, please share. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T12:35:48-08:00","id":1530193,"title":"","content":"This has always been something I\u2019ve struggled with tbh. Even in legacy I\u2019ve never been fully comfortable with the Fenrir uniquely having a wolf-manifestation for their tribal totem while every other tribe has a distinct totem and the rejection of Wolf in favor of tribal totems is supposed to be a significant thing.<br /> <br /> The problem is, at least for me, that Wolf, in some form or another, does fit most of my ideas about the Fenrir. While of course Fenris Wolf is a key part of their inspiration but also the image of the man-wolf warbands, koryos clad in wolf pelts and so forth is part of how I understand the Fenrir. I\u2019m not certain what I\u2019d replace it with.<br /> <br /> On one hand, I like Raven. Raven has war and death aspects, which would fit my idea of the Fenrir. On the other hand it would require some rewriting of the tribe\u2019s relationship with both the Corax breed and the mythological figure of Odin/Wotan. Then I think Bear, which has some promise as Bear has the berserker association and invoked the image of pre-historic Bear Cults and can be imagined with war and death aspects, particularly with Cave Bear as a guardian of caverns. On the other hand this would require dealing with the tribe\u2019s relationship with Gurahl and the Bear spirits relationship with the Garou in general. Wild Hound would be interesting and keep the koryos connotations I like and could invoke images like dog guardians of the underworld but it also smacks a bit of domestication and is still pretty close to wolf. Horses and Boars both have prominent roles in Norse myth but tbh I feel like those are more aligned with the Black Furies and Fianna. Well, maybe Boars could be work. They have the reputation for aggression and ferocity, plus the rooting for mushrooms could be given a spiritual connotation but then there\u2019s the Grondr question and for me Boars just don\u2019t quite feel right - they have a more Celtic vibe to me for some reason. Serpents could be interesting but then again there\u2019s the Wyrmish connotations and also that Older Brother/Ghost Council already has something in that vein.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I\u2019m open to ideas and suggestions. I suppose Boar and Bear might work best, although I still have a soft spot for Raven. I\u2019m really not sure tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T12:48:46-08:00","id":1530195,"title":"","content":"Reminder: The All-High is apparently still a thing in W5. So... you'd need to do a lot of rethinking everything about Odin, because he's still a vampire, and contrary to what W5 thinks, Garou didn't go after them in pre-W5 because they used Sense Wyrm on them and picked up something. It's because vampires are double, triple, and up bastards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T14:12:41-08:00","id":1530203,"title":"","content":"I most definitely agree with the characterisation of pre-Cult Fenrir as a Tribe of Glory: one noted that there were fewer tribes of Glory than of Honour &amp; Wisdom (A nicely symbolic evocation of the darker tone in this edition, Glory being in shorter supply).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also perfectly convinced that the Cult of Fenris is, as cultists often are, either wilfully delusional or lying their tails off about Wolf being their Patron Spirit - it makes perfect sense that a movement/body proclaiming themselves the True Warriors of Gaia (with an undertone that they\u2019re the only REAL Warriors of Gaia) would claim a special connection to the spiritual progenitor of all werewolves, therefore asserting their primacy over those that follow \u2018lesser\u2019 totems and those werewolves who must <i>obviously</i> be \u2018less wolf\u2019 than the werewolves actually being blessed by Wolf.<br /> <br /> It actually struck me while reading through the list of Gifts in 5th Edition that Dire Wolf would be a near-perfect pick for the Patron Spirit of the Cult (and presumably the tribe from which they erupted): a prehistoric spirit of an animal that\u2019s huge and inspiringly wolf like \u2026 but which might not actually be a wolf, going by some recent scientific studies.<br /> <br /> I therefore respectfully recommend Dire Wolf as totem for the pre-Cult Fenrir (and possibly for the Cult of Fenris itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T14:34:17-08:00","id":1530205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530203#post1530203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I most definitely agree with the characterisation of pre-Cult Fenrir as a Tribe of Glory: one noted that there were fewer tribes of Glory than of Honour &amp; Wisdom (A nicely symbolic evocation of the darker tone in this edition, Glory being in shorter supply).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also perfectly convinced that the Cult of Fenris is, as cultists often are, either wilfully delusional or lying their tails off about Wolf being their Patron Spirit - it makes perfect sense that a movement/body proclaiming themselves the True Warriors of Gaia (with an undertone that they\u2019re the only REAL Warriors of Gaia) would claim a special connection to the spiritual progenitor of all werewolves, therefore asserting their primacy over those that follow \u2018lesser\u2019 totems and those werewolves who must <i>obviously</i> be \u2018less wolf\u2019 than the werewolves actually being blessed by Wolf.<br /> <br /> It actually struck me while reading through the list of Gifts in 5th Edition that Dire Wolf would be a near-perfect pick for the Patron Spirit of the Cult (and presumably the tribe from which they erupted): a prehistoric spirit of an animal that\u2019s huge and inspiringly wolf like \u2026 but which might not actually be a wolf, going by some recent scientific studies.<br /> <br /> I therefore respectfully recommend Dire Wolf as totem for the pre-Cult Fenrir (and possibly for the Cult of Fenris itself).</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Aenocyon dirus</i> definitely wasn't a wolf as we know it. More like a swole dhole that was terrible at running long distances. It also lived entirely within the Americas, and died out about the time the Impergium started (at least for the pre-W5 timeline of the Impergium).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T14:46:15-08:00","id":1530207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530164#post1530164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, that was kind of my general idea--getting away a little bit from the Get of Fenris as the ultimate warriors to the [Get] being badass survivalists who seek adversity to burn away any remaining weakness in them. That being their ethos, I saw their role in Garou society both as vanguard/shock troops, as community enforcers, and as martial and athletic teachers.<br /> <br /> However, I'm still very open to completely alternative ideas. So, if you have another good suggestion, please share. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>How about going with a split of Bear the Healer and Bear the Warrior? The tribe that would form the nexus of the Cult used to balance the two poles, the Bear as Nurturer and healer, and the Bear as furious machine of destruction. In their pain, outrage and frustration they turned away from Bear the Nurturer, and Bear the Warrior without the balancing act of its children lost its way. What remains of the tribe that is the core of the Cult now follows Bear the Nurturer and seeks to heal the hearts of their fury driven brethern and bring their Patron back into a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T15:02:53-08:00","id":1530210,"title":"","content":"I'm going with Conquer/Forge/Prevail. For patron spirit, I know it's going to sound weird, but what about the dragon? In some adaptations the dragon is seen as an almost invulnerable creature, but in others it is seen as a creature that is born alone and has to adapt to live and when it survives a major confrontation it grows and develops stronger and with harder scales, which can be used as a parallel to the Get wish of power and valuing their scars. I know it's a bit silly, but it's a point to think about, Imao.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T07:15:47-08:00","id":1530270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530205#post1530205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Aenocyon dirus</i> definitely wasn't a wolf as we know it. More like a swole dhole that was terrible at running long distances. It also lived entirely within the Americas, and died out about the time the Impergium started (at least for the pre-W5 timeline of the Impergium).</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s noted in the WtA 5th edition core book that certain Gifts (Native Gifts, if memory serve, the equivalent to the old Breed Gifts) are taught by Dire Wolf spirits, so Dire Wolf seems<br /> to remain a going concern in the Umbra (In the same way that Lion, totem of the White Howlers, wasn\u2019t the Modern lion).<br /> <br /> I\u2019d argue that Dire Wolf technically not being a wolf at all would work perfectly as a means of showing how the Cult of Fenris represents a distortion (A dangerous, possibly dangerously-deluded distortion at that) of beliefs held by the Tribe that went before it.<br /> <br /> Under this paridigm, Dire Wolf would represent not only Aenocyon dirus but every primordial wolf-beast, probably with an extra helping of the vargr from Norse myth: wolves so hungry they will someday chew their way through the very heavens and the old gods of the North.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T08:03:36-08:00","id":1530275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530270#post1530270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s noted in the WtA 5th edition core book that certain Gifts (Native Gifts, if memory serve, the equivalent to the old Breed Gifts) are taught by Dire Wolf spirits, so Dire Wolf seems<br /> to remain a going concern in the Umbra (In the same way that Lion, totem of the White Howlers, wasn\u2019t the Modern lion).<br /> <br /> I\u2019d argue that Dire Wolf technically not being a wolf at all would work perfectly as a means of showing how the Cult of Fenris represents a distortion (A dangerous, possibly dangerously-deluded distortion at that) of beliefs held by the Tribe that went before it.<br /> <br /> Under this paridigm, Dire Wolf would represent not only Aenocyon dirus but every primordial wolf-beast, probably with an extra helping of the vargr from Norse myth: wolves so hungry they will someday chew their way through the very heavens and the old gods of the North.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unwilling to entertain typographical errors from AD&amp;D Monstrous Compendium releases as carry-overs into modern horror and action-horror games. Especially when, again, as an animal that was only ever living on Turtle Island, they would never have been seen in days past except by the Three Brothers, and their memory should likely only continue on among the Mokole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T08:04:57-08:00","id":1530276,"title":"","content":"(With regard to typographical errors, dire wolves in AD&amp;D 1e were actually the size that their remains said they should be - M, shorter than a timber wolf but bulkier. Wargs in 1e were size L. Come 2e, they suspiciously switched sizes.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T04:47:32-08:00","id":1530364,"title":"","content":"To each their own.\ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T05:40:30-08:00","id":1530374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530164#post1530164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, that was kind of my general idea--getting away a little bit from the Get of Fenris as the ultimate warriors to the [Get] being badass survivalists who seek adversity to burn away any remaining weakness in them. That being their ethos, I saw their role in Garou society both as vanguard/shock troops, as community enforcers, and as martial and athletic teachers.<br /> <br /> However, I'm still very open to completely alternative ideas. So, if you have another good suggestion, please share. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have an idea for an alternative Patron-Spirit that could be used instead to go along with what you describe: The wolf-mother or she-wolf. With the main-reference being the wolf who raised Romulus and Remus. And in keeping with that you could rename the Tribe the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lupercal\" target=\"_blank\">Lupercal</a>. And the main-traits are as you describe a focus on raising one's strengths and virtues through overcoming adversity with a secondary trait being that you help those who are struggling to overcome adversity until they can do so on their own. There's the focus on individual strength, so there's still a bit of the warrior-Tribe in there but it's now tinged with a focus on protection and guiding others.<br /> <br /> Then again, this still raises the issue of having a heavily wolf-focused theme which is a bit on the nose for a bunch of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T14:18:22-08:00","id":1530481,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to let you know that I <i>really</i> appreciate all your great responses so far, but my creative juices are still fermenting at the moment, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I like the she-wolf idea, but you convinced me that having a wolf spirit as the patron spirit seems weird when all the other tribes have other patrons. (I'm fine with Fenris being a patron for the Cult, assuming it's a destructive spirit, keen on wreaking havoc on the cosmos).<br /> <br /> Looking at the different tribe patrons again, we have three types of patrons: mythical beasts (Gorgon, Unicorn, Horned Serpent, Griffin), animals (Rat, Stag, Spider, Owl, Falcon), and natural phenomena (North Wind, Thunder). Among the Glory tribes, we have one of each so far. Maybe we have been looking into the wrong direction? What about a tree for a patron? Oak, for instance, for its association with longevity, strength, fertility, and robustness; also it's importance in Germanic cultures, or it's association with Perk\u02b7\u016bnos...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm still thinking, but please continue to brainstorm as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T14:42:13-08:00","id":1530484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530481#post1530481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to let you know that I <i>really</i> appreciate all your great responses so far, but my creative juices are still fermenting at the moment, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I like the she-wolf idea, but you convinced me that having a wolf spirit as the patron spirit seems weird when all the other tribes have other patrons. (I'm fine with Fenris being a patron for the Cult, assuming it's a destructive spirit, keen on wreaking havoc on the cosmos).<br /> <br /> Looking at the different tribe patrons again, we have three types of patrons: mythical beasts (Gorgon, Unicorn, Horned Serpent, Griffin), animals (Rat, Stag, Spider, Owl, Falcon), and natural phenomena (North Wind, Thunder). Among the Glory tribes, we have one of each so far. Maybe we have been looking into the wrong direction? What about a tree for a patron? Oak, for instance, for its association with longevity, strength, fertility, and robustness; also it's importance in Germanic cultures, or it's association with Perk\u02b7\u016bnos...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm still thinking, but please continue to brainstorm as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have some trepidations about being too on-the-nose with a Patron-Spirit like the She-Wolf. I think the only way to make it work would be through a properly epic origin-story. You get away from the obviousness that exists on the surface by getting into the specifics of an epic story. By that I mean, turning the Patron-Spirit into more of a character and having an origin-story associated with the Tribe that is an actual story with arcs, protagonists, antagonists etc. You get away from the lame qualities that exist on the surface by having a specific story with specific characters to make it work.<br /> <br /> But that's more of a concept for a Tribebook, of course, than a pitch to make this work as an in-game faction during a game. I think you can overcome it via good stoyrtelling and worldbuilding but it needs work. And of course, what's even cooler is to have worldbuilding that doesn't require big amounts of storytelling and lore to make it work. So that's why the wolf-focus is a bit of an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T19:42:08-08:00","id":1530526,"title":"","content":"The other issue with having She-Wolf as the patron spirit is that the ban is that hips can't lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T13:12:02-08:00","id":1530583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530526#post1530526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other issue with having She-Wolf as the patron spirit is that the ban is that hips can't lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if we do that, the Cult of Fenris at least got to have the Ban that they always have to bite off the hand of someone when they Frenzy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T13:23:59-08:00","id":1530585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530583#post1530583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, if we do that, the Cult of Fenris at least got to have the Ban that they always have to bite off the hand of someone when they Frenzy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>No joke, this lycanthropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T03:14:56-08:00","id":1530627,"title":"","content":"You charming rascals are giving me mental images of a Viking Shakira \u2026 \ud83e\udd70","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T11:21:29-08:00","id":1530656,"title":"","content":"\u2026 and I want to thank you for the gift!<br /> <br /> Wait a minute, where did Monday go to?!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T00:46:27-08:00","id":1530790,"title":"","content":"So, after some thinking, I'm partial to choosing Wild Boar (or simply Boar) as the tribe patron for the [Get].<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It's not a wolf patron.</li> <li>Boars are a species that can be found on all continents (even if their not native) and it's an invasive species, corresponding with the tribe's tendency to conquer new territory. Suidae can be found all across the globe.</li> <li>Across different cultures, wild boars have been associated with warrior virtues, aggressiveness, fierceness, toughness, power, but also avarice and recklessness--all fitting for a warrior and survivalist tribe. I also like that the tribe is a bit &quot;pigheaded&quot; and sees/saw itself as the Garou police (&quot;pigs&quot;).</li> <li>Boars are social animals, and mothers will aggressively defend their young. Going back to the function/renown matrix, this could represent the community aspect of the tribe.</li> <li>In Legacy, Boar was one of the totems associated with the Get of Fenris.</li> </ol>I'm not too worried about the association of boar with the Grondr for two reasons: First, it's not even clear whether there ever were Grondrs in W5. Second, if there ever were, they are extinct now.<br /> <br /> The only thing I don't really like is that it's yet another animal patron.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe you have additional ideas how to match the boar patron with the direction suggested by the function/renown matrix? Also, do you have any suggestions for nuances with regard to the tribe's character? Tribe verbs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T11:44:22-08:00","id":1530833,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering: Do we still wanna keep the Norse-part? Because if so, the Norse-reference that I think would be appropriate is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hildisv%C3%ADni\" target=\"_blank\">Hildisvini</a>. Not only is it a war-boar but it's also a shapeshifter since it's actually Freyja's protege Ottar (which would be a good association with the werewolves as shapeshifters). It also would take the Tribe in a more benign direction than its association with Fenris (at least on the surface because the Revised Tribebook did take some steps to establish its own logic for the Fenris-connection).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T22:29:56-08:00","id":1530871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530833#post1530833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering: Do we still wanna keep the Norse-part? Because if so, the Norse-reference that I think would be appropriate is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hildisv%C3%ADni\" target=\"_blank\">Hildisvini</a>. Not only is it a war-boar but it's also a shapeshifter since it's actually Freyja's protege Ottar (which would be a good association with the werewolves as shapeshifters). It also would take the Tribe in a more benign direction than its association with Fenris (at least on the surface because the Revised Tribebook did take some steps to establish its own logic for the Fenris-connection).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the established anti-myths in Revised. Fenris is right, the Aesir and Vanir are wrong, and we flip the assumptions on their head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T02:35:57-08:00","id":1530882,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but if we're restarting at zero, is it really worth it? Essentially what gets presented is a mythological reference while also saying that the myth is inaccurate. So you're pointing at a reference but also say it isn't that. &quot;It's Fenris - but not the Fenris you know.&quot; And then you have to deal with this added step of explaining what this is supposed to mean. And WtA doesn't consistently do that, as well. There's no subversion in the portrayal of the Griffon, for example. So I wonder if it wouldn't be better to just ditch that conceit of an anti-myth. Maybe if all the mythological were handled in the same way, it could work where you say that human beliefs/stories in general just get it wrong and the Garou know the truth. But since WtA doesn't do that, I think just picking a Patron Spirit that's more suitable on the face of it works better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T11:29:31-08:00","id":1530916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530882#post1530882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but if we're restarting at zero, is it really worth it? Essentially what gets presented is a mythological reference while also saying that the myth is inaccurate. So you're pointing at a reference but also say it isn't that. &quot;It's Fenris - but not the Fenris you know.&quot; And then you have to deal with this added step of explaining what this is supposed to mean. And WtA doesn't consistently do that, as well. There's no subversion in the portrayal of the Griffon, for example. So I wonder if it wouldn't be better to just ditch that conceit of an anti-myth. Maybe if all the mythological were handled in the same way, it could work where you say that human beliefs/stories in general just get it wrong and the Garou know the truth. But since WtA doesn't do that, I think just picking a Patron Spirit that's more suitable on the face of it works better.</div> </div> </div> </div>W:tA actually does have declarations of that right in its foundations. Humanity is largely presented as ignorant of how the world works, and disconnected from the truth of the Umbra. The problems come in when it has to reconcile the opinions of every different author, or when other games throw their weight around or write something a certain way.<br /> <br /> And the subversion with Griffin is like the subversion with Mokole (and Dragon, through them) - the monsters don't hoard gold, but humans think that because of a common incapability to learn of &quot;beast guards a precious treasure&quot; and not think that it's wealth (rather than unspoiled territory or memories of what Was). Even the gold-obsessed Firedrake has packs destroy it instead of collecting it and physically bringing it somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T22:16:07-08:00","id":1530949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530833#post1530833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering: Do we still wanna keep the Norse-part? Because if so, the Norse-reference that I think would be appropriate is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hildisv%C3%ADni\" target=\"_blank\">Hildisvini</a>. Not only is it a war-boar but it's also a shapeshifter since it's actually Freyja's protege Ottar (which would be a good association with the werewolves as shapeshifters). It also would take the Tribe in a more benign direction than its association with Fenris (at least on the surface because the Revised Tribebook did take some steps to establish its own logic for the Fenris-connection).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good question. No, I don't think it's in the spirit of the new edition to keep the Norse references and connections of the older editions. Tribes in W5 are defined by their relationship with their patron spirit, not by human cultures/ethnicities or geographical regions.<br /> <br /> However, I wouldn't mind if there were historical examples of significant tribe members that correspond to some culture or region. So, even if the [Get] were to be a global tribe, there could be a specific [Get] viking warrior from the 9th century who epitomizes the ideals of the tribe still today. Nevertheless, even if there were tribe heroes like this, they probably wouldn't influence the tribe culture as a whole.<br /> <br /> Then again, just like with certain professions, you will have selection effects though. That is, people from cultures that celebrate certain virtues (in the past or present) will be drawn to a tribe that shares them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T01:08:42-08:00","id":1530956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> I'm wondering: Do we still wanna keep the Norse-part? Because if so, the Norse-reference that I think would be appropriate is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hildisv%C3%ADni\" target=\"_blank\">Hildisvini</a>. Not only is it a war-boar but it's also a shapeshifter since it's actually Freyja's protege Ottar (which would be a good association with the werewolves as shapeshifters). It also would take the Tribe in a more benign direction than its association with Fenris (at least on the surface because the Revised Tribebook did take some steps to establish its own logic for the Fenris-connection). </div> </div> </div>So, I had a long hashing out of this with my writing team, and at the end of the day, we decided there are real life cultural representations of societies that espouse many of their ideals without having to be explicitly 'nordic'. In short, the baltic countries, or slavs, hold to a strong culture of resistance and hospitality. Their origins are rooted in being slaves, and developed a viciousness in having to resist both the russian and germanic tribes that sought to control them, while openly accepting anyone into their numbers that espouse their ideals. They do not seek a senseless death for it's own death, but rather, a cause worthy of dying for. They believe in strong communities, capable leaders, and sacrifices of meaning. And as a big plus, if you include all baltic countries in this demographic, it includes nordic folk as well; no need to change the name or patron. Glyph used with permission from Feral Noesis. Here's a brief writeup we put together in a preview chapter for Werewolf: the Essentials:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Bookletter 1911\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/Jc3Iyla9-ylNurqq8w3_IX6tq1iHYXsbPYg3gT8D8SQpVi4OG_DiIl4zYlg8P4BSADyabQPoA-GJGqBrldBaFk1LoMJ3z9Sun5HjV2SDTF6y0LElEpGjwm__YpQrtCF7kUdad-6ZBEGJTpC1q5wM2WM\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/Jc3Iyla9-ylNurqq8w3_IX6tq1iHYXsbPYg3gT8D8SQpVi4OG_DiIl4zYlg8P4BSADyabQPoA-GJGqBrldBaFk1LoMJ3z9Sun5HjV2SDTF6y0LElEpGjwm__YpQrtCF7kUdad-6ZBEGJTpC1q5wM2WM\" data-thumb-url=\"https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/Jc3Iyla9-ylNurqq8w3_IX6tq1iHYXsbPYg3gT8D8SQpVi4OG_DiIl4zYlg8P4BSADyabQPoA-GJGqBrldBaFk1LoMJ3z9Sun5HjV2SDTF6y0LElEpGjwm__YpQrtCF7kUdad-6ZBEGJTpC1q5wM2WM\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span></span> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\">Get of Fenris</span></b></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#434343\"><i>We clawed, we chained, our hearts in vain</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><i>We jumped, never asking why</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><i>It slowly turned, you let me burn</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><i>And now, we're ashes on the ground</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\">\u2014 Miley Cyrus \u201c</span><span style=\"color:#434343\"><i>Wrecking Ball\u201d</i></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Bookletter 1911\">Blood and sacrifice are how the Fenrir measure both their own worth and the worth of others. Bloodshed in the war against their enemies, and the blood ties that join them as a tribe. They battle against the Wyrm and battle to defend their loved ones. The Get give no quarter, and expect none. Their actions speak louder than words, granting leadership to those most capable of leading. No material sacrifice is made without cost, and no prayer or oath is spoken without personal investment in it\u2019s success. The saying, \u201ctrue warriors never grow old,\u201d is taught to all Fenrir cubs as an ideal of both the immortality of legends, and the dishonor of cowardice.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Bookletter 1911\">They are a practical tribe with a history of resistance and hospitality, never hesitating to speak from the heart. Warriors defeating insurmountable odds that have passed down their traditions through the generations, forged in blood, enduring their baltic origins as former slaves and animistic pagans. In the modern day, Fenrir pay homage to these old heroes as tacticians, commandos, and battle masters.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Bookletter 1911\">The Get do not save their ferocity only for doing battle, however, as they are a tribe that has a fierce reputation of upholding and defending their own kinfolk. Warriors are the most fit to lead in battle, and family the most fit to lead the household. They defer to their kin families as the zedakhs on the homefront \u2014 anyone wishing to raise their voice in discussion is afforded respect</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":27167,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","user":"mundusartis","date":". 02-16-2024, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T20:34:05-08:00","id":1531085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1530956#post1530956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I had a long hashing out of this with my writing team, and at the end of the day, we decided there are real life cultural representations of societies that espouse many of their ideals without having to be explicitly 'nordic'. In short, the baltic countries, or slavs, hold to a strong culture of resistance and hospitality. Their origins are rooted in being slaves, and developed a viciousness in having to resist both the russian and germanic tribes that sought to control them, while openly accepting anyone into their numbers that espouse their ideals. They do not seek a senseless death for it's own death, but rather, a cause worthy of dying for. They believe in strong communities, capable leaders, and sacrifices of meaning. And as a big plus, if you include all baltic countries in this demographic, it includes nordic folk as well; no need to change the name or patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, this is still too regionally bound for my taste. I thought about keeping the Norse/Germanic influences and, with Latvian grandparents on one side and East Prussian grandparents on the other, I thought about including Baltic influences as well. Still, I don't think it's the way to go.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I'd also be careful about throwing Balts together with the Norse. P\u0113rkons/Perk\u016bnas may be the equivalent of Thor, but so is Zeus (in the sense that all three probably have the same Proto-Indo-European origin). The rest of Latvian and Lithuanian native religion is quite different (Estonian even more so, as far as I know). Latvia (as an example that I know a little about) has always been the plaything of Germany, Russia, and Sweden, so for the Balts it's very important to retain their specific identity.<br /> <br /> ===<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm very busy lately, but I'll try to generate a rough outline of a tribe write-up and post it here for feedback soon.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T06:52:45-08:00","id":1531112,"title":"","content":"I guess the only role I can see for tying things to ethnicities and cultures is to use it as a reference for worldbuilding and to explain the history of a Tribe. So you're saying &quot;A Garou-Tribe is a homogenous collection of Garou and Kin/Kinfolk that settled down in a specific region and by doing so this Garou-community intermingled with the peoples and cultures of that region. And this has led to humans and Garou influencing each other in what their practices and beliefs are like. And then throughout history, things changed, people moved, cultures shifted and with that, the Tribe spread out as well.&quot; And in addition to that, you have the whole Ancestor-aspect. So no matter where your Fenrir was born in the 21st century, their identity ties back to the Norse/Germanic culture through their Ancestor-spirits. Like when an Irish-American claims Ireland as part of their identity even though they were born in the US and have always lived there but through the origins of their ancestors, they now claim &quot;Irishness&quot; as part of their identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T11:17:06-07:00","id":1532382,"title":"","content":"Sorry for having disappeared there for a while... I'm about to get ready for writing up the tribe, but I have some ideas to float here first.<br /> <br /> So, I gave the tribe the tentative name of <b>Bloodrazors </b>(an alternative would be the <b>Crimson Tusks</b>). Here are two glyphs I smashed together for the tribe and its patron spirit Boar. (I know there was a Grondr glyph, but I couldn't make sense of it.)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/OeUGjrP.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> What do you think of the name and glyphs? Love it, neutral, hate it?<br /> <br /> It's easier to do the write-up if I have a name for the tribe, so that's why I want this out of the way first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T08:01:32-07:00","id":1532500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1532382#post1532382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for having disappeared there for a while... I'm about to get ready for writing up the tribe, but I have some ideas to float here first.<br /> <br /> So, I gave the tribe the tentative name of <b>Bloodrazors </b>(an alternative would be the <b>Crimson Tusks</b>). Here are two glyphs I smashed together for the tribe and its patron spirit Boar. (I know there was a Grondr glyph, but I couldn't make sense of it.)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/OeUGjrP.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> What do you think of the name and glyphs? Love it, neutral, hate it?<br /> <br /> It's easier to do the write-up if I have a name for the tribe, so that's why I want this out of the way first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, long time lurker.<br /> <br /> I prefer the Crimson Tusks for a Tribe name. It fits the two name framework of most of the names in W5.<br /> <br /> The Tribal glyph works and I can easily see the source for the blood and tusks. Boar is a bit more confusing. The Beast of War glyph is really throwing me off, so I am curious as to why you chose it? I've always interpreted the Grondr glyph as a boar facing the left with its head down rooting in the earth. You could add two more short marks to get four &quot;legs&quot; making it a bit more obvious?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T09:05:16-07:00","id":1532507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1532382#post1532382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of the name and glyphs? Love it, neutral, hate it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be a personal perception issue, but the right glyph doesn't rorschach as 'boar' to me, but 'snail'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*writes down 'weresnail' into idea notebook*</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T09:26:56-07:00","id":1532509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1532382#post1532382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for having disappeared there for a while... I'm about to get ready for writing up the tribe, but I have some ideas to float here first.<br /> <br /> So, I gave the tribe the tentative name of <b>Bloodrazors </b>(an alternative would be the <b>Crimson Tusks</b>). Here are two glyphs I smashed together for the tribe and its patron spirit Boar. (I know there was a Grondr glyph, but I couldn't make sense of it.)<br /> <br /> What do you think of the name and glyphs? Love it, neutral, hate it?<br /> <br /> It's easier to do the write-up if I have a name for the tribe, so that's why I want this out of the way first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Having thought about this... I also like Crimson Tusks more as a name.<br /> <br /> But here are a couple more suggestions (and also categories that could serve as inspiration for other suggestions):<ul><li>The first is less a category by itself but more about the name in relation to the other Tribe-names. With blood and crimson, you have the color red and Red Talons already cover that. Then again you also have Black Furies and Shadow Lords. But I just wanted to mention it as a category to keep in mind.</li> <li>Natural phenomenons or minerals: Like Iron Tusks or Storm Razors.</li> <li>Emotions: Tusks of Wrath</li> <li>Ditching the boar-connection for the Tribename for something more neutral (and then recombine that with the second element like Crimson etc.): Stalwarts..., Vanguard..., Protectors...</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T11:09:57-07:00","id":1532513,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1532500#post1532500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tribal glyph works and I can easily see the source for the blood and tusks. Boar is a bit more confusing. The Beast of War glyph is really throwing me off, so I am curious as to why you chose it? I've always interpreted the Grondr glyph as a boar facing the left with its head down rooting in the earth. You could add two more short marks to get four &quot;legs&quot; making it a bit more obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually the war glyph (Silver Records, p. 109) which is almost identical to the Beast of War glyph. So, I see how it might be confusing... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1532507#post1532507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be a personal perception issue, but the right glyph doesn't rorschach as 'boar' to me, but 'snail'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was that it resembles the head of a boar. But it's good to know if this doesn't come across.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8wIzVgX.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T11:12:16-07:00","id":1532514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1532509#post1532509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having thought about this... I also like Crimson Tusks more as a name.<br /> <br /> But here are a couple more suggestions (and also categories that could serve as inspiration for other suggestions):<ul><li>The first is less a category by itself but more about the name in relation to the other Tribe-names. With blood and crimson, you have the color red and Red Talons already cover that. Then again you also have Black Furies and Shadow Lords. But I just wanted to mention it as a category to keep in mind.</li> <li>Natural phenomenons or minerals: Like Iron Tusks or Storm Razors.</li> <li>Emotions: Tusks of Wrath</li> <li>Ditching the boar-connection for the Tribename for something more neutral (and then recombine that with the second element like Crimson etc.): Stalwarts..., Vanguard..., Protectors...</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>These are all great. I have to think about it. If the others want to chime in on this, feel welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T11:27:09-07:00","id":1532516,"title":"","content":"Overlaid on the boar image, it's now obvious!<br /> <br /> I'd still maybe play around with it a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T12:23:28-07:00","id":1532518,"title":"","content":"We already have a glyph for boar;<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://imgur.com/a/QiNBNBv\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://imgur.com/a/QiNBNBv\" data-thumb-url=\"https://imgur.com/a/QiNBNBv\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img width=\"227\" data-align=\"left\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://imgur.com/fhHEqOG\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://imgur.com/fhHEqOG\" data-thumb-url=\"https://imgur.com/fhHEqOG\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_left js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:unset\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/fhHEqOG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/fhHEqOG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/fhHEqOG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T01:41:44-07:00","id":1532690,"title":"","content":"First draft for the write-up (up to the patron spirit). Feel free to critique away...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Boycott\"><span style=\"color:#70392b\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Crimson Tusks</span></span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Only the strongest survive and thrive. I am here to forge you into an unbreakable instrument of war for Gaia\u2019s glorious last stand.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Once a powerful</span> and proud tribe, the Crimson Tusks have fallen far since the rise of the Cult of Fenris. In the past, they viewed themselves as the Garou Nation\u2019s vanguard, fearless warriors conquering new territory and forging the way for the other tribes, keeping order and control among their brethren, while teaching them how to be strong and unyielding.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Today, the tribe is all but extinct, not because of a danger from without, but because they were betrayed by their disillusioned elders. Led astray by the dread spirit Fenris, most tribe members abandoned their tribe\u2019s patron spirit and joined the Apocalypse Wolf\u2019s nihilistic death cult.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Crimson Tusks in play might expect to <b><i>prevail</i></b> through extremely harsh circumstances, <b><i>conquer</i></b> a caern that fell to Black Spiral Dancers, <b><i>enforce</i></b> the rulings of their sept elders, or <b><i>forge</i></b> the next generation of Garou into deadly warrior.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Who are the Crimson Tusks?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If one were to ask the remaining Crimson Tusks about their tribe, they would tell grandiose stories how they were the ones keeping the Garou Nation together. Without their oversight, their strict enforcement of the Litany, their teachings of strength and resilience, their eradication of weakness and impurities, the other tribes lost their way and drifted apart. The other tribes would tell another story, however\u2026 the Crimson Tusks have always been a tribe of extremes, they would say, prone to belligerence and pigheadedness, excessive violence, blind obedience, and authoritarianism. The truth likely lies somewhere inbetween those views.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>What doesn\u2019t kill you, will make you stronger. Gaia can only be saved and avenged by the strongest of the strong.</i> For the Crimson Tusks, strength and survival are everything. The strength to prevail can only grow from adversity, however, and the Crimson Tusks revel in seeking it out. The Apocalypse is happening right now, and the Wyrm\u2019s servants know no mercy. Thus, the Crimson Tusks feel their teachings have to be harsh and indifferent, like nature itself, forcing those around them to adapt and to grow more resilient\u2026 or die trying. For a Crimson Tusk, there is nothing worse than weakness \u2014 in themselves or others \u2014 and they do everything to eliminate any perceived impurities.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This obsession with strength made them into one of the fiercest tribes of the Garou Nation. Whenever the opportunity arose to prove their mettle, the Crimson Tusks volunteered to be the vanguard, seeking glory by charging ahead into the fray without fear or doubt. Often, Crimson Tusks were the driving force behind conquering new territory or facing their enemies head-on, even if the odds seemed against their favor.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Their combative natures and hierarchical thinking in terms of strength and weakness often strained their relationship with the other tribes, especially the Black Furies and Children of Gaia. At the same time, some tribes, particularly the Silver Fangs and the Shadow Lords, knew how to utilize these characteristics to their advantage: in many septs, Crimson Tusks were tasked with keeping law and order, enforcing the Litany and keeping the peace, but \u2014 in reality \u2014 exerted control over the sept as the leaders\u2019 enforcers. After all, it\u2019s harder to show dissension during a moot, if Crimson Tusk thugs keep breathing down your neck.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Despite being irritated by the Crimson Tusks\u2019 dubious Social Darwinist outlook and exhausting combativeness, many Garou had to begrudgingly acknowledge the results. That is, these characteristics tended to forge Crimson Tusks into peerless, tough-as-nails warriors. Thus, Crimson Tusks often were allowed a more benevolent role in septs as well, teaching young Garou how to accept conflict and adversity as parts of their lives, how to increase their prowess enough to survive, how to defend themselves against a multitude of enemies, and how to become unbothered by the curveballs that life tends to throw at you, instead viewing them as opportunities to grow.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T02:02:23-07:00","id":1533157,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Patron Spirit</span></b><br /> <br /> Boar is the patron spirit of the Crimson Tusks, a mighty spirit associated with power, toughness, fierceness, and stubbornness \u2014 all desirable virtues for a tribe of relentless warriors. However, Boar is also known for his avarice and recklessness. Hunters fear Boar\u2019s children for good reason: they are too angry to pass up a challenge, to fierce to ever give ground, and to ornery to die before doing massive damage. Boar and the Crimson Tusks are associated with Glory.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#70392b\"><b>Favor:</b></span>Boar demands his children become tough warriors withstanding any hardship and making their enemies tremble in fear. Crimson Tusks may add a die to any dice pool involving Brawl, Intimidation, or Survival, as long as they stand their ground.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Ban:</span> </b>Boar is proud and stubborn, punishing those harshly who don\u2019t live up to his expectations. If a Crimson Tusk yields to an adversary, even if it makes sense strategically, or shows weakness and vulnerability before others, they may recover only a single Willpower at the start of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> </span>[For my house rules: Tribe Favor = Brawl, Intimidation, Survival]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T03:09:56-07:00","id":1533159,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Crimson Tusk Archetypes</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#496e43\"><b>Adrenaline Junkie</b></span><br /> You noticed something off with you from early on; you only felt truly alive with your heart racing and adrenaline shooting through your body. You started with freerunning and city parkour, but soon craved more: Bungee jumping, motocross, canyoning, cave diving, hang gliding, ice climbing\u2026 there is hardly an extreme sport you haven\u2019t tried and loved. Yet, this itch, this need for the rush always returns even stronger. Now that your supernatural regeneration has removed off any sense of danger from most activities, you cannot help but wonder\u2026 what does it take to make you feel alive again? How far do you have to push in the fight against the Wyrm to feel at peace? Your pack has already confronted you about how you\u2019re becoming more reckless by the day.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Tyrannical Deputy Sheriff</span></b><br /> There are those who cannot wait to escape their small town in order to seek refuge in the city. You never understood them. You love the cozy feeling of familiarity, safety, acknowledgement, and predictability there. A feeling of home, of territory \u2014 and of control. You protect your territory and its people, keep law and order, but you\u2019re not taking kindly to any troublemakers or outsiders. After all, it\u2019s your town and your rules! Sure, some may think you\u2019re a busybody who sticks their nose into their private business. What they don\u2019t understand is the simple fact that everything in this town is <i>your</i> business. You are its protector, its guardian. Their reluctance doesn\u2019t matter, however\u2026 they will fall in line, eventually, and they will learn to appreciate you.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Drill Instructor</span></b><br /> You\u2019re not a sadist, despite what some may claim. You don\u2019t derive pleasure form being merciless on your students whatsoever. After all, they aren\u2019t responsible for their weaknesses. No, it\u2019s their parents, their previous teachers, their society who are to blame. You will not fail them as well, however! No matter the reasons, you will forge your students\u2019 impurities out of them until they turn into a steel worthy of Gaia\u2019s fight. At the beginning of the training, your students usually don\u2019t appreciate their lessons. When those who fought their first battles return to you, however \u2014 a haunted look in their eyes, marked by the horrors of war \u2014 you spot gratitude in their eyes. They know what you did for them. And, in return, you reward them by showing your pride about their accomplishments.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">MMA Champion</span></b><br /> You have always been a fighter, a survivor. Maybe it was growing up on the streets that made you this tough? Whatever the reasons, you\u2019re good at beating people into pulp, breaking their bones and spirits. The best at it, in fact. After taking up boxing and Brazilian jiu-jitsu, others soon took notice. Your trainers were all over you, calling you an outstanding once-in-a-lifetime talent, dragging you from tournament to tournament, sponsor to sponsor. It all happened in a flurry, really. You didn\u2019t care. You never wanted to be a martial arts champion, you never wanted to be rich and famous. You just wanted to keep on fighting. It\u2019s the only thing you know, the only thing that makes you happy. After your First Change, you had to retire from professional sports to protect the Veil, but now you have found your true calling. Now, the fight will never end again. Hell yeah!<br /> </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T04:13:14-07:00","id":1533161,"title":"","content":"Quick question from someone who has never read W5<br /> <br /> Were the Get of Fenris once a real tribe whose members all fell to Hauglosk in W5, or did they never exist at all in this setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T05:03:10-07:00","id":1533163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1533161#post1533161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question from someone who has never read W5<br /> <br /> Were the Get of Fenris once a real tribe whose members all fell to Hauglosk in W5, or did they never exist at all in this setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the Get aren't called that. There was a tribe that had Wolf as its patron. Not much else is established so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:30:35-07:00","id":1533192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1533161#post1533161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question from someone who has never read W5<br /> <br /> Were the Get of Fenris once a real tribe whose members all fell to Hauglosk in W5, or did they never exist at all in this setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how it's described in the W5 corebook: &quot;The Cult of Fenris is itself but a single facet of a greater tribe pledged to Wolf, but the Cult raised its collective voices louder, and those pledged to Wolf either joined them or found membership among the other tribes.&quot; But the Cult of Fenris is also both treated like a Tribe of its own in W5 and a movement you can join as a member of another Tribe (at least, if you follow the portrayal of the Deepest of Wounds adventure by Renegade).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:53:31-07:00","id":1533208,"title":"","content":"The wording on that is such a set of bloody fingerprints. &quot;We're not going to <i>say</i> that it was the Swords of Heimdall of the Get of Fenris, <i>but</i>...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T22:48:46-07:00","id":1533736,"title":"","content":"I've just returned from a 10-day meditation retreat and, at the beginning, I couldn't help but think a bit about the Cult of Fenris... specifically, what is my house-ruled Cult of Fenris supposed to be really about.<br /> <br /> I already established that the Cult is a nihilistic movement of which many members have fallen into hauglosk (specifically, my house-ruled &quot;lashing out due to hopelessness&quot; version).<br /> <br /> I had an idea that I want to float here: The Cult came into being when Fenris, a spirit of chaos and destruction (so, basically Wyld-Wyrm), approaches the Crimson Tusk leadership and explains them that the Wyrm has been caught in the Weaver's web, and its madness lies in that &quot;it thinks&quot; it can remain in a constant and stable stage of self-digestion/consumption which never ends. Because the Weaver has warped it, it expects a static and eternal cycle of destruction without destroying itself eventually. However, if Gaia were to end, the Wyrm would need to eat itself as well. So, Fenris tempts the Crimson Tusks with an opportunity to become agents of the Wyld-Wyrm to destroy the faulty setup and to basically &quot;reboot&quot; the cosmos. So, accelerationist basically.<br /> <br /> This would mean that the BSD become more servants of the Weaver-Wyrm, whereas the Cult becomes an ally of the Wyld-Wyrm (or sane/Balance Wyrm, depending on how you interpret it).<br /> <br /> The offer Fenris would have made to the Crimson Tusks and all Garou who join them is to give them the resources (Banes, Gifts, etc.) that follow the path of ultimate destruction and rebirth, not just the flawed vision of the Weaver-tainted Wyrm.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 04-07-2024, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T01:51:06-07:00","id":1534325,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is a first draft: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/tf07k22tjqvyxgiqw011l/Crimson-Tusks-v00b.pdf?rlkey=48us4bvlzg4z1h1sxx71c3tsr&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/tf07k...xx71c3tsr&amp;dl=0</a><br /> <br /> I'd be really grateful for your feedback. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, next step would be to create the original Crimson Tusk gifts. I've already chosen the five Auspice Gifts and will have a look at the legacy Get of Fenris and Grondr Gifts next. Still, if you have any cool ideas, I'd be happy about some input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 04-17-2024, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T04:19:34-07:00","id":1534330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1534325#post1534325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here is a first draft: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/ajzax27jmv8ptv25w8q46/Crimson-Tusks-v00.pdf?rlkey=jdwnppxv2n5egbqhrsj00isgs&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/ajzax...rsj00isgs&amp;dl=0</a><br /> <br /> I'd be really grateful for your feedback. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, next step would be to create the original Crimson Tusk gifts. I've already chosen the five Auspice Gifts and will have a look at the legacy Get of Fenris and Grondr Gifts next. Still, if you have any cool ideas, I'd be happy about some input.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor one, but did you hire the W5 tribe artist to do the pictures??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T04:42:42-07:00","id":1534334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1534330#post1534330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Minor one, but did you hire the W5 tribe artist to do the pictures??</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's all AI art photoshopped by me.<br /> <br /> I commission art for other RPGs (mostly Mark Smylie, to be fair). This is purely for my home games and myself, however, so I'm not willing spending money on it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T04:54:55-07:00","id":1534335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1534334#post1534334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's all AI art photoshopped by me.<br /> <br /> I commission art for other RPGs (mostly Mark Smylie, to be fair). This is purely for my home games and myself, however, so I'm not willing spending money on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe remove it, since you are directly stealing from the artist's style using AI. I know the artist traces, but AI is just plain ol' stealing, especially in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T06:23:51-07:00","id":1534337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1534335#post1534335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe remove it, since you are directly stealing from the artist's style using AI. I know the artist traces, but AI is just plain ol' stealing, especially in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fundamentally disagree with you that it's &quot;stealing&quot;. First of all, I didn't copy the artist's style, I used &quot;gouache&quot; as a style. Second, the style is similar but different. Third, that it looks like in the rulebook was my digital work, using the raw materials that AI had generated, not the AI.<br /> <br /> However, since it seems to cause offense, I grayed out the picture for the version uploaded here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T20:57:06-07:00","id":1534383,"title":"","content":"You know it would be interesting if the Cult of Fenris is actually serving an &quot;uncorrupted&quot; aspect of the wrym, or to be more accurate this aspect of the wrym is suffering from a different type corruption than what we're familiar with.<br /> <br /> Instead of wanting to pollute the Gaia and escape it's prison like the other aspects, this aspect want to outright destroy everything, Weaver, Wyld, Gaia her self, even it's own existence. It doesn't care as long it's free form it's own suffering. Also contrary what the beings few supporters say, It doesn't care if the world can recover from it's destruction as part of some &quot;great cycle&quot; nor would it care if the concept of recantation is obliterated from existence by it's own hand. <br /> <br /> As long as there is silence then it's content. <br /> <br /> <br /> Hell you can even say that Hauglosk is caused by it's influence or at least it's influence exacerbated an pre existing condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T23:25:06-07:00","id":1534385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1534383#post1534383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know it would be interesting if the Cult of Fenris is actually serving an &quot;uncorrupted&quot; aspect of the wrym, or to be more accurate this aspect of the wrym is suffering from a different type corruption than what we're familiar with.<br /> <br /> Instead of wanting to pollute the Gaia and escape it's prison like the other aspects, this aspect want to outright destroy everything, Weaver, Wyld, Gaia her self, even it's own existence. It doesn't care as long it's free form it's own suffering. Also contrary what the beings few supporters say, It doesn't care if the world can recover from it's destruction as part of some &quot;great cycle&quot; nor would it care if the concept of recantation is obliterated from existence by it's own hand.<br /> <br /> As long as there is silence then it's content.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hell you can even say that Hauglosk is caused by it's influence or at least it's influence exacerbated an pre existing condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's exactly how I see Fenris's agenda (see write-up). What I didn't make explicit is that, in my games, Fenris is a powerful spirit serving the Balance Wyrm. (It's phrased a bit differently because W5 tries to avoid anthropomorphizing the Triat.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T00:12:25-07:00","id":1534388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530138-w5-fixing-the-cult-of-fenris-and-creating-the-tribe-it-sprung-from?p=1534385#post1534385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, that's exactly how I see Fenris's agenda (see write-up). What I didn't make explicit is that, in my games, Fenris is a powerful spirit serving the Balance Wyrm. (It's phrased a bit differently because W5 tries to avoid anthropomorphizing the Triat.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah though I should note that this aspect of the Wyrm has a extremely skewed definition of &quot;balance&quot; since if every things dead then everything will be in balance. <br /> <br /> Also I suspect that only the leaders actually know that they're working with a aspect of the Wyrm while the lower members are ignorant and only know the Cult of Fenris as a organization that still serv gaia, just via much more extreme means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T22:58:36-07:00","id":1534543,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Crimson Tusk Gifts</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\"><u><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Total Renown 3</span></u></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Porcupine\u2019s Reprisal <i>(As Philodox) </i></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Resist Pain</span></b><br /> Through sheer grit, the Crimson Tusk is able to push through the pain of their wounds and continue acting normally. A bear-spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Renown:</span></b> Glory<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Cost:</span></b> 1 Rage Check<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Action:</span></b> Full<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Pool:</span></b> Resolve + Glory<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">System:</span></b> </span></span>The user\u2019s player makes a Gift test at a Difficulty of 2 + 1 for each level of Aggravated damage the Garou is currently suffering (if any). If successful, the Garou becomes immune to all Health-based penalties, such as Impairment.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Duration:</span></b> One scene<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Snarl of the Predator</span></b><br /> The Crimson Tusk lets out a feral snarl that terrifies opponents and cows them into submission. A wolf-spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Renown:</span></b> Glory<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Cost:</span></b> 1 Rage Check<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Action:</span></b> Minor<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Pool:</span></b> Charisma + Glory vs Composure + Insight<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">System:</span></b> The Garou\u2019s player makes a Gift test against one enemy within earshot and line of sight. The enemy resists with their Composure + Insight. If the enemy fails, they suffer a two-dice penalty to attack this Gift\u2019s user.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Duration:</span></b> Success margin in turns</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Total Renown 6</span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Erymanthian Tusks</span></b><br /> The Erymanthian Boar was an untamable beast of legend. Its tusks were known for cutting through armor, severing nets, and snapping weapons of hunters and warriors alike. Crimson Tusks with this Gift can slice through stone, steel, and other inanimate materials with ease. This Gift is taught by a Boar-spirit.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Renown:</span></b> Glory<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Cost:</span></b> 1 Rage Check<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Action:</span></b> Minor<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Pool:</span></b> \u2014<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">System:</span></b> The Garou adds twice their Glory rating for feats of strength that involve damage or destruction of an inanimate object using their natural weaponry.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Duration:</span></b> Once scene<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Fangs of Judgment </span><i><span style=\"color:#496e43\">(As Philodox) </span></i></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Heart of Fury</span></b><br /> The Garou can steel themself against anger, suppressing their Rage and creating a mental dam against any explosive outbursts. This anger will catch up with them eventually, though, so they must vent it before it breaks free. A boar-spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Renown:</span></b> Wisdom<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Cost:</span></b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Action:</span></b> Full<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Pool:</span></b> \u2014<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">System:</span></b> The Garou can ignore a number of Brutal Outcomes equal to their Wisdom rating. When the scene ends, however, past slights and injuries come rushing back to haunt the Garou, refilling their heart and soul. At the end of the scene, they must spend another Willpower point or make a frenzy check immediately at the regular difficulty.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Duration:</span></b> Once scene<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">TRUE FEAR <i>(As Ahroun)</i></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Total Renown 9</span></b></u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Defy Death <i>(As Galliard)</i></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Razorback\u2019s endurance</span></b><br /> The Garou is able to call upon Boar\u2019s incredible toughness. This powerful Gift grants the Garou great endurance and hardiness for a time. This Gift is taught by a Boar-spirit.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Renown:</span></b> Glory<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Cost:</span></b> 1 Willpower<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Action:</span></b> Free<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Pool:</span></b> \u2014<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">System:</span></b> The Garou\u2019s Stamina is increased by their Glory rating for the duration of the scene. This will aid any rolls involving Stamina, but also increase the Garou\u2019s Health levels. The additional Health levels count as natural and are subject to regeneration. In contrast to additional Health levels gained from Crinos form, any damage to these additional Health levels disappears together with them when the Gift ends. This Gift can be used only once per session.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#70392b\">Duration:</span></b> One scene<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Strength of Purpose <i>(As Philodox) </i></span></b></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 04-22-2024, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T23:42:03-07:00","id":1534681,"title":"","content":"For completion's sake, <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/5ckmkdh3pzf1lh1bhfap9/W5-Caldorian-s-House-Rules-v4.3b.pdf?rlkey=rvwzct74clqhlmyxhi44uho4k&amp;st=xm1ffbgl&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">this is probably the final shared version of my house rules</a>, for those of you who helped create them. Any further changes, I will only make based on my own playtests and won't necessary share them. In the end, it's all for my home games. Thanks again for the constructive advice and help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 04-27-2024, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}